course: dictionary
lesson: 4511
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: One word can have many meanings, and head is a good example. It can mean a part of your body, a leader, the front of something, or the side of a coin. The context tells you which meaning to use, so ask: what does the rest of the sentence tell me?
explain: «Ella turned her head to look at the swing.» Here head is the top part of your body, because you turn your head. But «The head of the line was already at the gate» uses head to mean the front part of a line, because it is about the front of the queue.
explain: «The children headed home.» Head as a verb means to go towards somewhere, and the word home is the clue. Swap in your meaning, "went towards", and check that the sentence still makes sense.
fact: Head can be a noun, a verb, or an adjective: a head of lettuce, to head home, or a head teacher.
fact: «Head» means the top part of your body, with your eyes, nose, mouth, ears and brain.
fact: «Head» can mean the leader or the person in charge, as in «head teacher».
fact: «Heads» means the side of a coin with a face on it, as in «heads or tails».
fact: «Head» can also mean to hit a ball with your head.
exercise: «The Great Sphinx is a huge statue with a lion's body and a pharaoh's head.» What does head mean here? | To go towards | *The top part of the body, with eyes, nose and mouth | The leader in charge | The side of a coin
exercise: «Hammerhead sharks swing their heads from side to side as they search.» What does heads mean here? | The leader in charge | The side of a coin | To go towards somewhere | *The top part of the body
exercise: «The head of the table was empty.» What does head mean here? | The part of your body with eyes and ears | The side of a coin | To hit a ball | *The top or front part of something
test: «The head teacher read the notices in assembly.» What does head mean here? | A part of your body | To go towards | *The leader in charge of the school | The side of a coin
test: «The children headed for the park after school.» What does headed mean? | Was the leader | *Went towards | Counted | Hit with the head
exam: «Badger peered out of a hedge with «a stripy head».» Which meaning of head is it? | To hit a ball with the head | The leader in charge | The side of a coin | *The top part of the body
